>
> **Дальше:** ожидание разбудит меня, когда вкладка остановится; я сразу напишу вам, а затем сам перезапущу тесты на итоговом коммите, прежде чем называть что-либо зелёным.
>
> **От вас:** ничего.
>
> Проверено: ничего нового. На боевых машинах изменений нет. Голосований с прошлого статуса не было. Бэклог: <ссылка на Artifact>

## Why

- **Background waiter:** the brief was already delivered and the tab is working, which is the one case for a separate `herdr agent wait` (§3). The dispatch itself should have been a single background call; this re-arm repairs that.
- **Timeout:** 2700000 ms is the 45-minute upper end of the time box. A timeout is itself news.
- **No watching:** a foreground wait blocks me and caps at 10 minutes. A screen or `agent get` loop is polling, and it burns context I cannot spare at 58%.
- **Last week's missed notice:** it came from my being busy, not from the mechanism. Tonight nothing is queued, so I stay free.
- **The operator's wish:** "before I sleep" waives no gate (§8, §10). I state the real sequence so they can decide about sleep themselves. It needs no poll because I am asking nothing.
- **"Still running":** a running agent has no result, and its screen is not a report (§12). A mid-run "tests passed" line can precede a failing step or come from a stale commit, so I re-run the decisive check myself (§11).
